{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets, and the census file: how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786914783610},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to calculate how many farmers markets the U.S. has per 100,000 residents. I need to:\n\n1. Get the total number of farmers markets from the first dataset\n2. Get the total U.S. population from the census file\n3. Calculate the ratio per 100,000 residents\n4. Verify all calculations using xorq tools\n\nFirst, I should orient myself by checking the semantic models and any existing aliases in the catalog. The project instructions say to run `xorq_semantic_models` and `xorq_catalog_list_aliases` FIRST.\n\nLet me start by checking what's in the catalog.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you find the farmers markets per 100,000 U.S. residents. Let me start by checking the catalog for existing semantic models and aliases."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_012fhJTAtqk7KUe7xY9ZvHZb","name":"xorq_semantic_models","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01EAB77rdyg7MgrVFWkoD9vF","name":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":10,"output":301,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":8157,"totalTokens":8468,"cost":{"input":0.000009999999999999999,"output":0.001505,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0.01019625,"total":0.011711250000000001},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":150},"stopReaso